==English==
{{was wotd|2019|April|27}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*krewh₂-}}
From {{der|en|LL.|recrudescentia}}, from {{der|en|la|recrūdēscēns}}, {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|recrūdēscere||to recrudesce}}, from {{m|la|recrūdēscō||to become raw again}}; from {{m|la|re-|t=again}} + {{m|la|crūdēscō||to grow harsh or violent; to become worse}} (from {{m|la|crūdus||bleeding, bloody, raw}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*krewh₂-||blood outside the body}}) + {{m|la|-ēscō|pos=''suffix forming verbs indicating a becoming of something''}}). The word is cognate with {{cog|fr|recrudescence}}, {{cog|it|recrudescenza}}, {{cog|es|recrudescencia}}, {{m|es|recrudecimiento}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=159984|date=June 2009|nodot=yes}}; {{R:Lexico}}</ref>

